Description: Fix CVE-2026-44496 ReDoS / cookie-name mismatch in cookies.read()
 cookies.read(name) built a RegExp by interpolating the caller-supplied cookie
 name directly into the pattern string. An attacker-influenced name containing
 regex metacharacters could trigger catastrophic backtracking (ReDoS) or match
 an unintended cookie. This replaces the RegExp-based lookup with a literal
 split/compare over document.cookie, matching only on an exact cookie name.
 .
 Note: the upstream fix also adds coverage in test/specs/helpers/cookies.spec.js,
 but the published npm tarball for this package does not ship a test/
 directory, so that hunk is omitted here — only the runtime fix in
 lib/helpers/cookies.js applies to the distributed source.
Origin: backport
Bug: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jp-ww65-95wh
Author: Patch Platoon <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-08-10

